        {"source": "spec", "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (`CAN0`, `CAN1`), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller (`U8`, `U9`) through an isolated CAN transceiver (`U11`/companion)"}
      ],
      "impact": "Shorting GND1 and GND2 defeats the galvanic isolation of the CAN transceivers, potentially creating ground loops, reducing noise immunity, and exposing the CM4/CAN-controller side to bus-side ground faults or transients.",
